---
components: ["TimeRangePicker"]
description: Time range picker sets one time range for a page of charts, from presets such as the last seven days or from two dates.
---

<script>
  import { createTimeRange, LineChart, TimeRangePicker, withinRange } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const NOW = new Date(2026, 9, 24, 9, 41).getTime();
  const HOUR = 3_600_000;
  const range = createTimeRange({ presets: ["24h", "7d", "30d"], initial: "7d", now: () => NOW });
  const all = Array.from({ length: 30 * 24 }, (_, i) => ({
    time: new Date(NOW - (30 * 24 - i) * HOUR),
    revenue: Math.round(900 + Math.sin(i / 17) * 250 + ((i * 7919) % 180)),
  }));
  $: rows = withinRange(all, "time", $range);
</script>

`TimeRangePicker` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`.

It is the control for a `createTimeRange` store: a `ContentSwitcher` of the store's presets, with a range `DatePicker` behind "Custom". See [Dashboards](/dashboards) for the store, the URL, and the charts that read it.

## Basic

Pass the store as `range`. Presets are a count and a unit, `m`, `h`, `d`, or `w`, written as "Last 7 days".

<TimeRangePicker {range} />

<LineChart data={rows} x="time" y="revenue" title="Revenue" xDomain={[$range.from, $range.to]} height={200} legend={false} />

## Presets only

Set `custom` to `false` to offer the presets alone.

<TimeRangePicker {range} custom={false} />

## Labels

`presetLabel` writes a preset your way, and `customLabel`, `fromLabel`, `toLabel`, and `placeholder` name the rest.

<TimeRangePicker {range} presetLabel={(preset) => preset.toUpperCase()} customLabel="Pick dates" />
